# Two broken operators in one pipeline give two errors; the rest of the tree is usable.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..44
  PIPELINE@0..43
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..20
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..20
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "a"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        EQ@17..18 "="
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        LITERAL@19..20
          LONG@19..20 "1"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
    PIPE@21..22 "|"
    WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
    PROJECT_OP@23..32
      IDENT@23..30 "project"
      WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@31..32
        NAME_REF@31..32
          IDENT@31..32 "b"
    WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
    ERROR@33..34
      IDENT@33..34 "c"
    WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
    PIPE@35..36 "|"
    WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
    TAKE_OP@37..43
      IDENT@37..41 "take"
      WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
      LITERAL@42..43
        LONG@42..43 "5"
  WHITESPACE@43..44 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | from t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
  |                  ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `a == 1`

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `c`
  --> query:1:34
  |
1 | from t | where a = 1 | project b c | take 5
  |                                  ^

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where a == 1 | project b c | take 5
which still has errors:

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `c`
  --> fixed:1:35
  |
1 | from t | where a == 1 | project b c | take 5
  |                                   ^
